---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import { site } from "../../lib/site";

const primaryCta = site.phoneNumber && site.phoneNumber !== "PHONE_NUMBER"
  ? { href: `tel:${site.phoneNumber}`, text: `📞 ${site.phoneNumber}` }
  : { href: "/contact/", text: "📞 Call for a Free Consultation" };

const signs = [
  { name: "Constant Regeneration", detail: "The unit regenerates far more often than its programmed schedule, wasting salt and water on every extra cycle." },
  { name: "No Regeneration at All", detail: "The control head never triggers a cycle, letting resin exhaust while hard water passes straight through." },
  { name: "Wrong Time or Day", detail: "Regeneration fires at the wrong hour or on the wrong day, usually pointing to a lost or drifting internal clock." },
  { name: "Display Errors or Blank Screen", detail: "An error code, frozen display, or completely blank screen signals a electronics or power-board fault inside the head." },
  { name: "Motor Grinding or Stuck", detail: "A control head motor that grinds, stalls, or fails to turn the internal piston prevents the valve from cycling correctly." },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Can a control head be reprogrammed instead of replaced?",
    a: "Yes — a drifting clock, wrong hardness setting, or incorrect regeneration schedule is a reprogramming fix, not a replacement, and takes under 30 minutes on a working head.",
  },
  {
    q: "When does a control head need full replacement?",
    a: "A cracked piston, failed motor, or dead circuit board on a unit over 10 years old is usually cheaper to replace outright than to source parts for, especially on discontinued models.",
  },
  {
    q: `Does control head failure mean the whole softener is done?`,
    a: `No. The resin tank and brine tank typically outlast the control head — a head swap on an otherwise sound system is a common, cost-effective repair in ${site.city}.`,
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title={`Water Softener Control Head Repair, ${site.city}`}
  description={`Signs your water softener's control head is failing, repair vs. replacement, and what a control head repair costs in ${site.city}.`}
>
  <PageHero
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Repair", href: "/repair/" }, { label: "Control Head Repair" }]}
    heading={`Control Head Repair in ${site.city}, ${site.stateAbbr} | Trusted Local Specialists`}
    primaryCta={primaryCta}
    secondaryCta={{ href: "/quote/", text: "Get a Free Quote" }}
  >
    <p slot="opening">
      Water Softener <a href="/" class="brand-link">{site.city} {site.state}</a>
      {" "}offers water softener control head repair and replacement across {site.city} and {site.county}. The
      control head manages regeneration cycles. A faulty control valve causes the softener to regenerate
      continuously, not at all, or at wrong intervals, passing hard water at {site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} GPG
      through untreated. Free diagnostic included with every repair call. All major control head brands
      diagnosed and serviced. Same day availability.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p>The control head is the electronic brain of a water softener — it tracks water use, triggers regeneration, and manages the internal piston that redirects water flow. At {site.gpgLow}-{site.gpgHigh} GPG, per {site.waterAuthority}, a {site.city} softener's control head cycles more often than in a softer-water market, which shortens its working life compared to city with lower hardness.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Five Signs of Control Head Failure</h2>
      <p>Five symptoms point specifically to the control head rather than the resin bed or brine tank:</p>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        {signs.map((s) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3>{s.name}</h3>
            <p>{s.detail}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p>See our full <a href="/repair/">water softener repair page</a> if your symptoms point to the resin bed or brine tank instead.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center">
        <h2>Repair vs. Replacement</h2>
        <p>Two factors decide which makes sense for a given control head.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Repair When...</h3>
          <p>The issue is a programming drift, a sensor fault, or a single replaceable part on a head under 10 years old — most control head calls fall into this category.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Replace When...</h3>
          <p>The circuit board or motor has failed on a discontinued model, or the head is original to a system over 12 years old and parts availability is limited.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>According to {site.waterAuthority}'s hardness data for {site.county}, most control heads in this market need attention between years 8 and 12 — get a free diagnostic to find out where yours stands.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Control Head Repair Cost in {site.city}</h2>
        <p>Reprogramming or a sensor fix typically runs $75 to $150. A motor or circuit board replacement runs $150 to $350 in parts and labor, and a full head swap on an aging system runs $250 to $500 — always with a written quote before work begins.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center">
        <h2>Control Head Repair Questions</h2>
        <p>Three questions come up most on {site.city} control head calls.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              {item.q}
              <svg class="faq-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 6.5 8 10.5 12 6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container final-cta">
      <h2>Control Head Acting Up in {site.city}?</h2>
      <p>Free in-home diagnostic with every repair call.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Book a Repair Call →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .faq-list { max-width: 760px; margin: 24px auto 0; }
    .final-cta { text-align: center; }
    .final-cta p { max-width: 48ch; margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
